; The punctuation, and the reason it is here: without it Smiles does not die,
; he stops being drawn.
;
; DRAWN FOR THE ROWS THAT SURVIVE. dd_rmap takes rows j*16/th, so a Hercules
; tile of 16x9 keeps master rows {0,1,3,5,7,8,10,12,14} and DROPS the other
; seven - and the first version of this was thin spokes and diagonals, every
; one of which fell in the gaps. It photographed as speckle. Four solid chunks
; flying apart survive any row map, because each is at least three rows deep,
; and the 3/2/6/2/3 banding here is symmetric at 16 and still has both gaps at
; 9.
